# AGENTS
1. INGESTION: normalize to schema; PII scrub to [EMAIL]/[PHONE]/[NAME]/[ID] into text_clean
   (keep original only if org retain_original=true); detect language (langdetect + script
   check + Hinglish/Tanglish word-list heuristic); normalize code-mixed text to English with
   the cheap model (mock = dictionary translator: thanda, garam, namak, kam, romba, illa,
   bekar, nalla...); dedupe by content_hash and rapidfuzz ratio>92 within item/day;
   return stats (received, cleaned, deduped, pii_scrubbed, by_language).
2. ANALYSIS (cheap model, batches of 20-30): per comment {feedback_id, sentiment, score -1..1,
   aspects[{aspect,sentiment}], issue_category (org categories or "other"/"none"), severity 1-5
   (1 minor, 3 clear failure, 5 health risk), entities{item,meal_type,location}, is_alert,
   alert_reason}. Prompt is templated from org_config; mixed comments pick the dominant
   category but list all aspects; prefer provided metadata over guessing entities. Validate,
   map unknown category to "other", re-request missing ids once. DETERMINISTIC ALERT BACKSTOP:
   final is_alert = LLM OR org keyword match (any language); create alerts rows. Mock = lexicon
   classifier per category (cold/thanda/thanni -> temperature, salty/oily/bland -> taste, ...).
3. INSIGHT: topic discovery over negative comments (current + prior 4 weeks) via embeddings or
   TF-IDF+KMeans (k 3-10 by silhouette); strong model names clusters (<=5 words + one-line
   summary) from representative comments only; counts and week-over-week trend computed by
   code; aspect breakdown table; persist topics.
4. PREDICTION: for each IssueKey(category,item,meal_type) build an evidence packet via
   build_issue_facts(); batch ~10 per strong-model call. LLM outputs risk High/Medium/Low,
   likely_day (only if dominant_share>=0.4), evidence items quoting exact field/value pairs,
   and a <=2-sentence rationale. NEVER percentages. Spikes cannot exceed Low without other
   evidence. Programmatically verify every cited value equals the packet; on mismatch retry
   once then fall back to the rule's reason; store evidence_verified. BACKSTOP:
   final_risk = max(llm_risk, rule_risk); never let the LLM lower a rule-High; note the floor.
   Produce plain-language forecast lines whose numbers match the data. Mock = rule + template.
5. PRIORITY (pure Python, no LLM): see formula below; attach open alerts as pinned items.
6. ACTION (strong model) for top N: concrete recommendation (specific to item/meal/day, no
   generic advice; hygiene gets containment + root-cause check), owner_role chosen from roles
   holding task.complete, effort 1-5, due date <=7 days (next occurrence of likely_day),
   measurable success_metric, evidence_refs. Validate owner/date/refs; re-run priority with the
   real effort; save as "proposed"; add a manager-facing "why". Mock = recommendation library.
7. VERIFICATION: see Phase 8.
8. REPORT & ALERT: see Phase 8.

# STATS TOOLS (pure pandas functions on DataFrames, every one takes as_of and filters
# timestamp < as_of so backtests cannot leak future data)
weekly_counts, weekly_rates (complaints/feedback), weeks_present(last_n=6), trend (slope
normalized by mean; needs >=4 points), day_of_week_pattern (+dominant_day/share),
days_since_last, avg_gap_days, complaint_rate, footfall_correlation, is_spike (one-week
exceedance of mean+2sd with other weeks near zero), before_after (rate-based, normalized by
volume, min sample sizes, enough_data flag), build_issue_facts (the evidence packet),
discover_issue_keys. rule_risk(facts): High if present >=4 of last 6 weeks OR (>=3 of 6 and
rising); Medium if 3 of 6 OR (2 of 6 and rising); else Low; spikes forced Low.
PRIORITY FORMULA: score = severity x org_weight x frequency(4-week count) x recurrence_weight
(High 3, Medium 2, Low 1) x reach / effort. PIN RULE: health_risk categories with severity>=4
or any open alert rank above all unpinned issues. Return score_breakdown + deterministic
explanation_text ("Ranked #1 because it is a hygiene risk").
BACKTEST: for each held-out week W use only data before W, predict, compare to whether the
issue actually recurred in W; report High precision, recall, confusion table, and a baseline
("recurs if it occurred last week"). The predictor is pluggable so the LLM agent can be
backtested too (add a --max-calls budget).

# LANGGRAPH WORKFLOW
State (TypedDict, small: IDs and summaries only; heavy data stays in DB): org_id, run_id, week,
as_of, org_config, ingestion_stats, alerts, topics, predictions, ranked, actions, approvals,
scheduled_tasks, verification_results, report, errors, node_timings, mode (full|verify_only).
Flow: ingestion -> analysis -> (conditional: new alerts -> alert node) -> insight -> prediction
-> priority -> action -> approval (HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP via interrupt(); resume with
Command(resume={approvals, approved_by}) after an action.approve RBAC check) -> schedule
(tasks only for approved actions, assigned to owner_role) -> verification -> report -> END.
verify_only mode jumps straight to verification -> report. Checkpointer SqliteSaver with
thread_id = f"{org_id}:{week}"; must resume after a process restart. Retry transient LLM errors
(max 2, backoff); Insight failure must not block Prediction; Analysis failure halts with a clear
error. @agent_node decorator logs start/end/duration and captures errors. Alert node never blocks
(email/Slack stubs log payloads unless webhook env is set; recipients hold alerts.receive).
Runner: start_run, get_run_status, resume_with_approvals, progress events for the UI.
CLI: python scripts/run_pipeline.py --org "ABC College" --auto-approve-top 3. Save the graph
diagram to docs/architecture.mmd. Re-running the same org/week must be idempotent.

