# VERIFICATION, IMPACT, YOU SAID WE DID, REPORTS (Phase 8 detail)
Verification runs when status=done and completed_at + VERIFY_AFTER_DAYS has passed. Use
before_after (14-day windows, rate-normalized). Verdict: insufficient_data if not enough data;
improved if relative drop >=30% AND absolute drop >= minimum; worse if rise >=20%; else no_change.
Add a two-proportion z-test confidence (high p<0.05, medium p<0.15, else low) and a confound
caveat if other items' overall complaint rate moved similarly. Strong model writes a 2-sentence
summary from the structured result only; code validates every number appears in the result. On
no_change/worse create a follow-up proposed action including the prior attempt. After a verified
fix, set fixed_on so build_issue_facts uses post-fix data and the key stops showing High forever.
P6 must verify as improved with a large drop; untouched P1 produces no verification.
Impact page: per-fix before/after chart (weekly rate with vertical marker at fix date, shaded
bands), verdict badge, numbers, sample sizes, confidence, caveats, owner and note; summary cards
(issues fixed, avg reduction, success rate, time to fix); admin CSV export.
You Said, We Did: public, student-voice entries ("You said: dosa on Monday mornings was cold. We did:
smaller batches and a warm tray. Result: cold-food complaints down 62%."), generated from anonymized
topic summaries (never raw comments), shown only if the manager ticks publish (default off); shareable
URL/QR and embed snippet; org name and accent color.
Weekly report: markdown with top issues/topics, satisfaction delta, forecast highlights, actions
proposed/approved/done, verification results, open alerts, overdue/escalations, "what to watch next
week". Code inserts all figures (validator checks numbers); LLM rewrites narrative only; export PDF and
.md; email via SMTP if configured, else log a stub.
Notifications: SMTP and generic webhook senders behind env flags (default stubs); alert text has severity,
item, meal, scrubbed excerpt, and a link to the Action Board. Escalations: proposed actions unapproved
past escalation_days, tasks past due, alerts unacknowledged past N hours -> escalation record, notify users
with users.manage or audit.view, banner on admin page, audit logged.
Scheduler (APScheduler): per-org weekly pipeline, daily verification, hourly escalation check, weekly
report; each org in its own try/except; idempotent; --run-now job_name CLI; /admin/jobs lists last/next run.

